      "text": "This module configures multi\u2011LLM access for Claude Code, exposing convenient wrappers:\n\n* Sets shared LiteLLM endpoint and key, and enforces safe token limits (CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=32000, MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0) needed for compatibility.\n* Defines `_CC_MULTILLM_ENV` with required Anthropic variables.\n* `ccfree` runs Claude Code against free cloud models via LiteLLM, mapping Opus/Sonnet/Haiku tiers to specific model names.\n* `cclocal` runs Claude Code entirely locally on an Ollama model (vibeforged\u201114b), requiring `olresume`.\n* `ccchore` starts a \u201cchore\u201d session that forces offload mode, automatically summarising large inputs via `llm`.\n* `llmcheck` reports the status of LiteLLM, Ollama, account, and health of isolated back\u2011end aliases without fallback, showing quota, cooldown, or errors.\n\nAll helpers are ready for on\u2011demand use via aliases.",
